# Water shores: land placed every other cell leaves one water cell between two islands, which must
# draw a shore on both sides (a channel), while the cells diagonal to both islands draw both corners.
# Then a cross of one-cell channels carved into a block of land: a crossing, four dead ends and the
# straight cells between. Then a two by two lake with a channel entering beside its shore. From the
# repository root:
#   cargo run -p HeritageBuilder -- --script crates/game/tests/scenarios/water_edges.jsonl
